  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the initial lead. The project has seen significant budget adjustments, starting with a $500,000 allocation for Phase One, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration, and ultimately approved for a total of $2M by the executive board to cover all phases. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics. Additionally, the project is exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology, and a compliance plan budget of $55,000 has been approved for training and audits. A detailed progress report will be shared in a staff meeting on November 20th."
